{"title":"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> below with the number you receive.\n</p><p>Calculate the sum of all the side lengths in the shape shown below.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the shape, we see that the sum of the sides is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/84004026f86b6ba7a10a752f0d29412f92476ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N + 7 + 4 + 3 = N + 11 + 3 = N + 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"306\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 2\">player 2</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22c8d367387129b104acc6092b079cde80451a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. Plugging this in, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb792c64a23318865912fb9a97fa5f53416221a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N + 14 = 3 + 14 = \\boxed{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"186\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC\">2021 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 2\">Practice Relay Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_4\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 4\">Practice Relay Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/